Our approach in the present work for proving the main theorem is following the general strategy originally introduced in the seminal work RiviereLin. It consists in looking for interpolation spaces estimates in neck regions. In fact this strategy allows for an up-grade of the energy quantization result to a much sharper $\mathrm{L}^{2,1}$ energy quantization; we record this as follows.

\begin{corollary} \label{L2quantization}
		There exists $\varepsilon_G, C_G> 0$ and $p_G>0$ such that for all $p\in[2,2+p_G]$ and for all $p$-Yang-Mills connection $A$ in $\mathrm{B}_R\backslash \overline{\mathrm{B}_r} $, for all $R,r$ with $0<r<4r<R<1$, if $A$ satisfies
		\[ \sup_{r \leq \rho \leq R /2} \| F_A \|_{\mathrm{L}^2(\mathrm{B}_{2\rho} \backslash \mathrm{B}_\rho)} \leq \varepsilon_{G}',\] then \[ \|F_A\|_{\mathrm{L}^{2}(\mathrm{B}_{R}\backslash \mathrm{B}_{r})} \leq C  \sup_{r \leq \rho \leq R/2} \| F_A \|_{\mathrm{L}^2(\mathrm{B}_{2\rho}\backslash \mathrm{B}_\rho)}\] and
		\[ \|F_A\|_{\mathrm{L}^{2,1}(\mathrm{B}_{R/2}\backslash \mathrm{B}_{2r})} \leq C  \sup_{r \leq \rho \leq R/2} \| F_A \|_{\mathrm{L}^2(\mathrm{B}_{2\rho}\backslash \mathrm{B}_\rho)}.\] 
	\end{corollary}

