theorem.content:
\label{cor:Grasssmannian}
Fix integers $1 \leq \ell < n$ and let $X = \mathrm{Gr}_{\ell,n}(\mathbb{R})$ be the Grassmann variety of $\ell$-dimensional subspaces in $\mathbb{R}^n$. Then there exists an explicit constant $\varkappa > 0$ and $\varepsilon > 0$ such that for $\sigma_X$-almost every $x \in X$, as $T \rightarrow + \infty$,
\begin{equation} \label{cor:eq_Grassmannian}
\mathcal{N}_{c, \beta}(x, T) = \varkappa \, c^d \, \ln (T) \left ( 1 + O_x(\ln(T)^{- \varepsilon}) \right ).
\end{equation}

