\end{equation}
Then, for every $f \in C_c(L/\Gamma)$, we have 
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{t\rightarrow \infty} \int_0^1 f(a(t)\psi(s)x_0)ds = \int_{L/\Gamma} f\, d\mu_L,
\end{equation}
where $x_0=e\Gamma$, $\overline{Gx_0}=L/\Gamma$, and $\mu_L$ is the unique $L$-invariant probability measure on $L/\Gamma$.

