$K[X_1,X_2,\dots, X_n]$ and let $G$ act linearly on the ring (fixing $K$). Assume that $|G|$ is invertible in $K$. We have $G\subseteq GL_n(K)$ is generated by psuedo-reflections if and only if $(K[X_1,X_2,\dots, X_n])^G$ is a polynomial ring over $K$.

