In recent years, considerable attention has been devoted to the fractional counterpart of De Giorgi's conjecture, in which the classical Laplacian in the Allen-Cahn equation is replaced by the fractional Laplacian. More precisely, one considers bounded entire solutions of
\begin{equation}\label{eq:fractional-AC}
 (-\Delta)^{s} u = u - u^{3} \quad \text{in } \mathbb{R}^{n}, 
 \qquad 0<s<1,
\end{equation}
