\label{thm:main_theorem}
Assume that there are constants $0 < b < R_* < R_0 < E$.
Let $T>0$ and $y_0 \in H_0^1(B_{R_0})$ radially symmetric. 
Then, putting $R(0)=R_0$, the three-dimensional free-boundary problem
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:PDE-intro}
\begin{cases}
 y_t - \Delta y + f(y) = 1_{\omega} u, & \text{in } Q_R, \\
y(x,t) = 0, & \text{on } \Sigma_R, \\
 y(\cdot,0) = y_0, & \text{in } B_{R(0)},
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
--
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:stefan_condition-intro}
R'(t) = -\nabla y(x,t) \cdot \hat n, \quad x \in \partial B_{R(t)},
\end{equation}
is locally null controllable.

