 \df{$\langle x \rangle$} denote the free monoid on the $\vg$ letters of the alphabet $x = \{ x_{1}, \dots, x_{\vg}\}.$ 
 Its multiplicative identity is the empty word 
 \df{$\varnothing$}. 
 We endow $\langle x\rangle$ with the \df{graded lexicographic order}.
 The length of a word $w \in \langle x \rangle$ is denoted by $|w|.$ The
 set of all elements (words) of $\langle x \rangle$ of length (or degree) at most $d$
 is denoted \df{$\langle x \ra_{d}$}.
 The cardinality of $\langle x\ra_d$ is \index{$N(d)$}
 \[
 N(d) \ =\ \sum_{i=0}^d \vg^i \ =\ \frac{\vg^{d+1}-1}{\vg-1}.
 \]

Let \df{$\mathcal{H}$} be a fixed complex Hilbert space.
 Let \df{$\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{H})$} be the space of all bounded linear operators on $\mathcal{H}$, and 
 let 
 \df{$\mathcal{A} $} to be the free semigroup $\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{H})$-algebra on $x,$
 i.e., $\mathcal{A}=\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{H})\langle x\rangle$. An element $p$ of $\mathcal{A}$ takes the form, 
 \begin{equation}\label{eq:poly}
 p \ =\ \sum_{w\in\langle x\rangle}^{\rm finite} P_{w} w,
 \end{equation}
