\label{thm:GWP}
Let $T>0$ and $\alpha\in[\alpha_{0},\,2]$, where $1.1108\approx\alpha_{0}\in (1,\frac{6}{5})$ is the root of the cubic equation $2\alpha^3+3\alpha^2-4\alpha-2=0.$

Assume that the initial data $u_0$ satisfies
\begin{align}\label{eq:init}
& u_0 \in \mathsf{H} \triangleq \Big\{ f\in L^{2}(\Omega): \int_{0}^{1}f(x,z)\,\mathrm{d} z=0,\,\,\forall\,x\in \mathbb{T}\Big\}, \quad  \Lambda_{h}^{\delta_m}u_0 \in L^{2}(\Omega),\nonumber\\
& \omega_{0}\triangleq\partial_{z}u_0 \in L^{\infty}(\Omega),\quad \Lambda_{h}^{\frac{3-2\alpha}{2}}\omega_{0} \in L^{2}(\Omega),\quad \text{and}\quad \partial_{z}\omega_{0} \in L^{2}(\Omega),
\end{align}
where
\begin{equation}\label{eq:deltam}
	\delta_m \triangleq \max \Big\{\frac{\alpha}{2},\,\frac{2(-\alpha^2-\alpha+3)}{3-\alpha}\Big\}.
\end{equation}
Then, the system \eqref{eq:main} with initial data $u_0$ has a unique global strong solution on $[0,T]$, with
\begin{align}\label{eq:sol}
& u\in C\big([0,T], \mathsf{H}\big),\quad \Lambda_{h}^{\delta_m}u \in L^\infty\big([0,T], L^{2}(\Omega)\big),\quad  \Lambda_{h}^{\delta_m + \frac\alpha2}u \in L^2\big([0,T], L^2(\Omega)\big),\nonumber\\
