There exists a pair $(\varepsilon_0,{\alpha_{0}})$ of positive constants that depend on the mass and energy of $F_{\mathrm{in}}^\varepsilon$, $m$, and $q$ introduced in
\begin{equation}\label{eq:defE}
\E:=L^1_v\W_x^{m,2}( {\m_q})\,, \qquad m > \frac{3}{2}\,, \quad q \geq 3+\g\,,\end{equation}
such that for $\varepsilon\in(0,\e_0)$ and if
$$\|h_{\mathrm{in}}^\varepsilon\|_{ \mathcal{E}} \leqslant {\alpha_{0}},$$
then, the equation
\begin{equation}\label{eq:heps} 
\partial_t h_\e + \frac1\e v \cdot \nabla_x h_\e + \xi_{\e}(t) \mathrm{div}_v (v h_\e) =
\frac{1}{\e^2} \LLe h_\e + \frac1\e \Q_{\e,t} (h_\e,h_\e) + S_\e(t,v)
\end{equation}
has a unique solution $h_{\varepsilon} \in\mathcal{C}\big([0,\infty); \mathcal{E}\big) \cap L^1_{\rm{loc}}\big((0,\infty);\E_1\big)$ 
satisfying 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:heZg}
\left\|h_\varepsilon(t)\right\|_{ \mathcal{E}}\leqslant \frac{C ({\alpha_{0}})}{\sqrt{1+t}}\,,
\qquad \forall \, t \geqslant 0\,, \qquad \forall \, \varepsilon \in (0,\e_0)\,,
\end{equation}
for some positive constant $C({ \alpha_{0}}) >0$ independent of $\varepsilon$. Moreover, the  solution splits as
\begin{equation}\label{eq:heps0+1}
h_{\varepsilon}(t)=\ho_{\varepsilon}(t)+\hu_{\varepsilon}(t)\end{equation}
and, for any $T >0$ there exists $\bm{h}\in L^{2}\left((0,T);\mathcal{H}\right)$ such that, up to extraction of a subsequence, it holds that
	\begin{equation}\begin{cases}\label{eq:mode-conv}
	\left\{\ho_{\varepsilon}\right\}_{\varepsilon} \text{converges to $0$ strongly  in } L^{1}((0,T)\,;{\E_1})\,, \\[0.2cm]
	\left\{\hu_{\varepsilon}\right\}_{\varepsilon} \text{converges to $\bm{h}$ weakly in } L^{2}\left((0,T)\,;\mathcal{H}\right)\,.
	\end{cases}\end{equation}
In particular, there exist 
	\begin{align*}
	\varrho \in L^{2}&\left((0,T)\,;\mathbb{W}^{m,2}_{x}(\mathbb{T}^{d})\right)\,, \qquad
	u \in L^{2}\left((0,T)\,;\left(\mathbb{W}^{m,2}_{x}(\mathbb{T}^{d})\right)^{d}\right)\,,  \\
	&\qquad\text{and} \qquad \vartheta \in L^{2}\left((0,T)\,;\mathbb{W}^{m,2}_x(\mathbb{T}^{d})\right)\,, 
