where $\mathcal M$ is the Maxwellian distribution
\begin{equation} \label{eq:max}
\M(v) :=(2\pi\en_{\star})^{-\frac{3}{2}}\exp\left(-\frac{|v|^{2}}{2\en_{\star}}\right)\,, \quad \forall\,v \in \R^{3}\,,
\end{equation}
and $(\varrho,u,\vartheta)=(\varrho(t,x),u(t,x),\vartheta(t,x))$ are suitable solutions to the following incompressible Navier-Stokes-Fourier system with forcing term
\begin{equation}\label{eq:NSFint}
\begin{cases}
\partial_{t}u-\frac{\nu_{0}}{\en_{\star}}\,\Delta_{x}u + {\en_{\star}}u\cdot \nabla_{x}\,u+\nabla_{x}p= \xi(t)\,u\,,\\[6pt]
\partial_{t}\,\vartheta-\dfrac{\nu_{1}}{\en_{\star}^{2}}\,\Delta_{x}\vartheta + \en_{\star}\,u\cdot \nabla_{x}\vartheta
