\label{FYZ}
Let $(M,\omega)$ be a compact K\"ahler manifold and $\chi$ a  closed real (1,1)-form such that the principal argument of  $\int_{M}(\chi+\sqrt{-1} \omega)^n$ is $\pi$. If there exists a smooth function $\underline{u}$ satisfying \eqref{subsolution},
