[Müller\&Vallarino \cite{MuVa}]\label{thm:MullerVallarino}
Let $S$ be a Damek–Ricci space of dimension $n$, and let $\mathcal{L}$ denote the left-invariant distinguished Laplacian and $\mathrm{d}\rho$ the right Haar measure on $S$. Then, for all $1<p<\infty$, there exists $C_p>0$ such that the solution to the Cauchy problem
\begin{align}\label{eq: wave}
\begin{cases}
\partial_t^2 u(t,x)-\mathcal{L} u(t,x)=0,
\qquad t\in\mathbb{R},\,x\in S,  \\
u(0,t)=f(x),\,\partial_t u(t,x)|_{t=0}=g(x),
\end{cases}
\end{align}
satisfies the estimate 
\begin{align}\label{est:mainthm}
\|u(t,\cdot)\|_{L^p(S,\mathrm{d}\rho)}
\leq C_p\,
\Big( (1+|t|)^{2|\frac{1}{p}-\frac{1}{2}|}\|(\mathrm{Id}+\mathcal{L})^{\frac{\alpha_0}{2}}\!f\|_{L^p(S,\mathrm{d}\rho)}+(1+|t|)\,\|(\mathrm{Id}+\mathcal{L})^{\frac{\alpha_1}{2}}\!g\|_{L^p(S,\mathrm{d}\rho)}\Big),
\end{align}
for all $t\in\mathbb{R}^*$, provided that 
\begin{align*}
\alpha_0>(n-1)\left|{1\over p}-{1\over 2}\right|
\quad\text{and}\quad \alpha_1>(n-1)\left|{1\over p}-{1\over 2}\right|-1.
\end{align*}

