ref_dict.lem:caccio:
\begin{theorem}[Caccioppoli inequality]\label{lem:caccio}
Let $\phi\in \Phiw(\Omega_T)$ satisfy \azero{},   \ainc{p} and \adec{q} for some $1<p\le q$, and 
parabolic \aone{}. Let
$u$ be a weak solution to the parabolic system \eqref{maineq} with growth \eqref{A-condition}. For any $a\in\mr^N$ and $Q_{r,\rho}(z_0)\Subset \Omega_T$ with $z_0=(x_0,t_0)$, 
$\tilde r \in (0, r)$ and $\tilde\rho\in (0, \rho)$, we have 
\[
\begin{split}
\underset{t \in (t_0-\tilde\rho,t_0+\tilde\rho)}{\mathrm{ess\,sup}}\int_{B_{\tilde r}}  |u(x,t)-a|^2\,dx &+ \int_{Q_{\tilde r, \tilde \rho}} \phi(z,|\nabla u|)\, dz \\
&\leq c\int_{Q_{r,\rho}}\left[\frac{|u-a|^2}{\rho-\tilde\rho}+ \phi\Big(z,\Big|\frac{u-a}{r-\tilde r}\Big|\Big)\right]\, dz
\end{split}
\]
for some $c=c(n,N,p,q,L,\Lambda)>0$.
\end{theorem}

