\begin{thm}\label{thm: main theorem}
    Let $X = G/\Gamma$  and $F = \{g_t : t\in\R\}\subset G$, where 
    \begin{itemize}
    \item $G$ is  a     Lie group with discrete center,
    \item $\Gamma$ is a non-uniform 
    lattice in $G$,
\item $g_t$ is as in \eqref{gt}, where $a_0 \in \fg\nz$ is $\ad$-diagonalizable over $\Co$;
 \item the action of $F$  on $(X,m_X)$ is mixing.
