    We let $H$, $H^-$ and $Z$ be the connected Lie subgroups of $G$ associated to the algebras $\fh$, $\fh^-$ and $\fn$ respectively. We fix $m_H$, a Haar measure on $H$. We further consider the connected subgroup $\tilde{H}$ associated to the Lie algebra $\fn \oplus \fh^-$ and a left Haar measure $m_{\tilde{H}}$ on $\tilde{H}$, scaled so that $m_G$ is a direct product of $m_H$ and $m_{\tilde{H}}$, see \cite[Ch.~VII, \S 9, Proposition 13]{B} or \cite[Theorem 8.32]{Kn} for justification.
