If we apply these results to the centralizers of elements in $G$, we obtain that a finite-dimensional definable group has the hereditary $\widetilde{\mathfrak{M}}_c$-property.
\begin{defn}
    A group $G$ is \emph{hereditarily-$\widetilde{\mathfrak{M}}_c$} if for any definable subgroups $H,N$, such that $N$ is normalised by $H$, there exist natural numbers $n_{HN}$ and $d_{HN}$ such that any sequence of centralisers 
    $$C_H(a_0/N)\geq C_H(a_0,a_1/N)\geq...\geq C_H(a_0,a_1,...,a_n/N)\geq...$$
