\begin{remark} \label[remark]{rem:limit-convention}
Here and throughout, any limit of $q$ or $N$ permits the parameters to vary and depend on each other arbitrarily unless explicitly stated otherwise. For example, the limit $q^N \to \infty$ includes the cases $q$ fixed with $N \to \infty$, $N$ fixed with $q \to \infty$, and more. 
