in a way that a quasi-conservative regime is predominant in order $1$ time-space variations. We note that the drift term in \eqref{BE0-In} effectively introduces energy in the rescaled granular gas, thus, a balance between the input-output energy fluxes along the hydrodynamic limit is a pre-requisite for the correct self-similar scaling.
As time evolves, a quasi-conservative regime is reached. This time scale depends on $\varepsilon$ since the number of collisions per unit time plays a central role in the dissipation process.
