&=\ud(f_0^*\omega_0)\wedge(f_1^*\omega_1)+(-1)^{\deg\omega_0}(f_0^*\omega_0)\wedge\ud(f_1^*\omega_1)\\
&=\ud(f_0^*\omega_0\wedge f_1^*\omega_1)=\ud f^*(\omega_0\otimes\omega_1)
\end{align*}
weakly. Consequently $f^*(\ud\tilde\omega_j)=\ud(f^*\tilde\omega_j)$ weakly. Now the pointwise convergence $f^*\tilde\omega_j\to f^*\omega$, $f^*(\ud\tilde\omega_j)\to f^*(\ud\omega)$ together with the dominated convergence theorem yield
