ref_dict.def:eigenproblem:
\begin{definition}[\(p\)-eigenvector]\label{def:eigenproblem}
We call \(u\in X\setminus\{0\}\) a \(p\)-eigenvector of \(J\) with subgradient \(\zeta\in  \partial J(u) \subset X^*\), duality map \(\partial H\), and eigenvalue \(\frac{J(u)}{H(u)} = \lambda\in\R\) if it fulfills the inclusion
\begin{equation}\label{eq:eigenproblem}
\zeta - \lambda\, \partial H(u) \ni0\,.
\end{equation}
\end{definition}

