ref_dict.defin:TopTrivialNC:
\begin{definition}\label{defin:TopTrivialNC}
Let $A$ and $B$ be separable nonunital \cstar-algebras, and let $\Phi\colon \mathcal Q(A)\to\mathcal Q(B)$ be a $^*$-homomorphism. We call $\Phi$ Borel if
 \[
\Gamma_\Phi= \{(a,b)\in \mathcal M(A)_{\leq 1}\times\mathcal M(B)_{\leq 1}\mid \Phi(\pi_A(a))=\pi_B(b)\}
 \]
 is Borel in the product of strict topologies.
\end{definition}

