\begin{theorem}\label{main thm 1}
Let $r\ge 2$ be an integer and $\chi$ be a primitive Dirichlet character modulo~$q$. Let $C(r)$ be defined as in Table \ref{Table 1}. Let $a(r) = 2\log{2}\left(3.0758r+1.38402\log(4r)-1.5379\right)$. Then, for $q \ge \max\{10^{1145},e^{e^{a(r)}}\}$, if $r=2$ or $q$ is cubefree, we have
