ref_dict.thm:acc=zeros:
\begin{theorem}\label{thm:acc=zeros}
Assume that for some $E\in \R$, $L^1(\omega,E)\geq \nu>0$.
Then for some $\gamma\in (0,1)$ and for $n$ large enough,
\begin{align}
\left| \frac{1}{2n} N_n (E,\delta/2)-\kappa^1(\omega,E)\right|\leq \delta^{-1} n^{-\gamma}.
\end{align}
\end{theorem}

