\begin{proposition}[Dumas, 2013]\label{prop:Dumas} Suppose that the spectral radius $\rho=\rho({\bf A})$ is the unique dominant eigenvalue of ${\bf A}$, that $\rho$ has equal geometric and algebraic multiplicities, and that $\rho({\bf A})>\rho^*({\bf A}_0,\ldots,{\bf A}_{k-1})$. Then, there exists a H\"older continuous 1-periodic function $\psi$ that is bounded away from zero such that \[\sum_{m\leqslant x}f(m) =\psi\big(\log_k(x)\big)\,x^{\log_k(\rho)}+o\big(x^{\log_k(\rho)}\big).\] 
\end{proposition}

