A related quantity, the minimal local time defined as $f(n)=\min\{\xi(s,n):s\in\mathcal{R}(n)\}$, was introduced by Erd\H{o}s and R\'{e}v\'{e}sz \cite{ER87,ER91} to study its $\limsup$ behavior. After a series of developments by T\'{o}th \cite{To96} and R\'{e}v\'{e}sz \cite{Re13}, our previous work \cite{FH25} ultimately established that
