 \end{align}
For any $\epsilon > 0$, assume that $\max\limits_{kN_1+1 \leq s \leq (k+1)N_1} g(s) \geq M$. Then there exists an integer $0 \leq i \leq \epsilon^{-1}$ with the property that
\begin{itemize}
 \item $g(kN_1) \geq \epsilon i M$,
 \item $\max\limits_{kN_1+1 \leq s \leq (k+1)N_1} \mathcal{G}_{kN_1,s} \geq (1 - \epsilon(i+1)) M$.
\end{itemize}
