Let \((M^n, g)\) be a complete, connected, and noncompact Riemannian manifold of dimension \(n\geqslant3\) with nonnegative Ricci curvature. Assume that \(f\in C(\mathbb R_+;\mathbb R_+)\) satisfies
\[\liminf_{v\to0^+}f(v)>0.\]
Then any positive supersolution to \eqref{Meq-gradient} must be constant.
\end{corollary}

\begin{corollary}
Let \((M^n, g)\) be a complete, connected, and noncompact Riemannian manifold of dimension \(n\geqslant3\) with nonnegative Ricci curvature. Then any positive supersolution to \eqref{eq-u^p} must be constant if \(p<2_*(q)-1\),
