\begin{prop}[{cf.~\cite[Corollary~3.4]{S78}}]\label{prop:ci}
Let $R$ be a standard graded $\kk$-algebra. 
If $R$ is a complete intersection, then the $h$-polynomial of $R$ is of type~CI, that is, $h_R(t)=\prod_{i=1}^r\Psi_{m_i}(t)$ for some non-negative integer $r$ and positive integers $m_1, \dots, m_r$.
\end{prop}

