Let $E_0\in \mathbb R$ be a fixed energy for which $L_d(\omega,E_0)>0$.
For any $\omega\in \mathrm{DC}$, the integrated density of states of $H_{\omega,\theta}$ satisfies
    \begin{align}
        |\mathcal{N}(\omega,E)-\mathcal{N}(\omega,E')|\leq |E-E'|^{\beta},
    \end{align}
    for any $E,E'\in I_{E_0}$, a neighborhood of $E_0$, and any H\"older exponent $0<\beta<1/(2\kappa^d(\omega,E_0))$.

