\begin{theorem}\label{thm_specialcase}
    Let $C$ be a genus $2$ curve with Jacobian that has multiplication by the maximal quaternion order with discriminant $6$, 
    and has field of moduli a number field $L$ with at least one real embedding. 
    Assume $C$ has potentially smooth stable reduction at primes above $2$ and $3$. Then its Jacobian has superspecial reduction at infinitely many primes. 
\end{theorem}

